Derived work notice

ZeaLead's architecture and its planner, worker and goal-decomposer prompts are adapted from
ARTEX, an autonomous penetration-testing platform licensed under AGPL-3.0:

    https://github.com/BaaRai/ARTEX
    Copyright (C) ARTEX contributors

The ideas adapted include the two linked graphs (shared source graph plus per-campaign exploration
graph), the event-driven planner with debounce, heartbeat and hard floor, single-intent workers with
an adversarial gate before reporting, verified evidence, early-proof refusal, the nonce-tagged
untrusted-data boundary, and the per-host noise governor.

The web console in web/ is adapted from the ARTEX web console: its layout, sidebar, theme presets,
preferences, UI components and the exploration-graph layout. ZeaLead's pages, API client and
domain components are new. The UI components derive from shadcn/ui (MIT License).

ZeaLead is distributed under the same license as ARTEX.

